{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>To rival.</b> From the root of וכעסת צרתה (and her rival shall provoke her). Now in the pericicle of Kedoshim he did not mention the punishment for one who lies with two sisters, just as he did not mention the punishment for one who lies with his son's daughter or his daughter's daughter. The commentator's reason is that Rachel and Leah were not sisters, and his proof is \"all these abominations,\" but this is not an absolute proof. And one who asks how HaShem could punish for a matter about which He did not warn — some answer that the children of Noah were commanded concerning these forbidden unions, and others say that even though Scripture said \"all these abominations\" as a general statement, the meaning is not about all of them but about most of them. My opinion you will know in the pericicle of Vayelekh Moshe."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:42.719719795Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}